# <%= it.scope %>/theme

The company's design tokens: everything in [`@mfeflow/theme`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@mfeflow/theme), plus
the light and dark tokens of this company and one helper that builds the themes. `/react` and `/starting` are
re-exported too. [`<%= it.scope %>/storage`](../storage) is installed with it: the chosen theme is kept in
storage, so the two are released together.

## What to fill in

`src/tokens.ts` holds the tokens in one file, `lightTokens` and `darkTokens`. Every name becomes a CSS variable
`--mf-<name>` on `<html>`, so keep the two lists on the same names. The values are starting points.

`createThemes()` returns `{ themes, defaultTheme }`: a `light` and a `dark` theme and `light` as the default.

In the shell:

```tsx
import { createThemes, noFlashScript } from '<%= it.scope %>/theme';
import { ThemeProvider } from '<%= it.scope %>/theme/react';

const { themes, defaultTheme } = createThemes();

// <ThemeProvider themes={themes} defaultTheme={defaultTheme}> ... </ThemeProvider>
// Put noFlashScript(themes, { defaultTheme }) in an inline <script> in the <head>.
```

In a remote, read the tokens with `var(--mf-color-bg)` or `cssVar('color-bg')`.

## Settings only, no state

`@mfeflow/theme` is a Module Federation singleton, shared by package name. `<%= it.scope %>/theme` is not in that
list, so every remote gets its own copy of this package while the one underneath stays shared. That is fine while
this package holds only settings and functions that build things. Keep it that way: no theme choice, listener
or flag at module level here. State belongs in `@mfeflow/theme` or in the shell.
